into the heart of the dodgeball Jabberwocky
that is the Globo Gym Purple Cobras,

910
01:03:18,773 --> 01:03:22,448
and walk away with $50,000
in stone-cold cash.

911
01:03:22,533 --> 01:03:26,492
Hello, everybody, and welcome
to what you've all been waiting for.

912
01:03:26,573 --> 01:03:30,248
A David-and-Goliath story
truer than the Bible itself.

913
01:03:30,333 --> 01:03:34,292
The championship dodgeball match
here on ESPN8 - the "Ocho".

914
01:03:36,893 --> 01:03:38,531
Peter?

915
01:03:40,773 --> 01:03:42,331
Peter?

916
01:03:42,413 --> 01:03:44,881
Hello?

917
01:03:44,973 --> 01:03:46,247
Peter?

918
01:03:46,333 --> 01:03:49,052
Come on, everybody headed down...

919
01:03:58,173 --> 01:04:00,004
So what happens on a double fault?

920
01:04:00,093 --> 01:04:05,247
On a double fault you go to sudden-death
elimination. It's Continuation Rule 113-D.

921
01:04:05,333 --> 01:04:07,972
- Whatever.
- Hey, guys, wait up.

922
01:04:11,813 --> 01:04:13,166
Justin.

923
01:04:13,253 --> 01:04:17,246
- I've been looking for you everywhere.
- Really? I mean, why? What's up?

924
01:04:17,333 --> 01:04:21,326
Derek fell off the roller coaster
and broke every bone in his body.

925
01:04:21,413 --> 01:04:22,812
My God, that's awful.

926
01:04:22,893 --> 01:04:26,329
We were the centre Kewpie. With no
centre Kewpie we can't do our routine.

927
01:04:26,413 --> 01:04:29,325
- No. I'm sorry.
- You gotta do it.

928
01:04:29,413 --> 01:04:31,005
What?

929
01:04:31,093 --> 01:04:33,084
No, no, no, no, no. I can't.

930
01:04:33,173 --> 01:04:36,882
Please. You are the only one in Las Vegas
who knows our routine.

931
01:04:36,973 --> 01:04:42,331
- The dodgeball championship's at noon.
- You'll be back in time. I promise.

932
01:04:45,253 --> 01:04:46,845
- All right, I'll do it.
- Yes.

933
01:04:46,933 --> 01:04:48,969
- I gotta tell the guys.
- No. No time.

934
01:04:49,053 --> 01:04:50,645
- I gotta tell the guys.
- No time.

935
01:04:52,453 --> 01:04:57,243
Average Joe's are a 50-1 underdog here today.
No one is giving them much of a chance.

936
01:04:57,333 --> 01:04:59,085
What do you think, Pep?

937
01:04:59,173 --> 01:05:01,243
I spoke to White Goodman before the match

938
01:05:01,333 --> 01:05:06,248
and he told me that his team
really wants to win this one.

939
01:05:06,333 --> 01:05:09,609
Right. And the stage is set for
Darwin's cruellest play to unfold.

940
01:05:09,693 --> 01:05:13,322
So don't go anywhere, folks.
The Schadenfreude is about to begin.

941
01:05:13,413 --> 01:05:17,565
- I don't understand. Why would Peter leave?
- He knows we're gonna get killed.

942
01:05:17,653 --> 01:05:22,727
Hey. That's not true. I don't know why Peter
left, but we can do this without him.

943
01:05:22,813 --> 01:05:25,885
We just have to figure it out.
Owen, you'll have to play.

944
01:05:25,973 --> 01:05:29,249
- OK, yeah.
- Great. But we'll still be two players short.

945
01:05:29,333 --> 01:05:33,292
We're still missing the teenage love-puppy
and Steve the Pirate.

946
01:05:33,373 --> 01:05:35,728
Who's Steve the Pirate?

947
01:05:35,813 --> 01:05:39,522
The only guy on our team
who dresses like a pirate.

948
01:05:39,613 --> 01:05:43,606
Wait. There's a guy on our team
dressed like a pirate?

949
01:05:45,133 --> 01:05:52,562
And now, let's hear it for the West Davenport
High School Charging Donkeys.

950
01:05:52,653 --> 01:05:54,644
Donkeys.

951
01:06:18,253 --> 01:06:19,811
Go, Donkeys.

952
01:06:22,533 --> 01:06:25,445
- We did it.
- Holy cow. My God.

953
01:06:25,533 --> 01:06:28,764
- It was perfect. You were perfect.
- God, I gotta go.

954
01:06:28,853 --> 01:06:31,048
Wait. Aren't you gonna stay for the trophy?

955
01:06:31,133 --> 01:06:33,806
I'm sorry, Amber. I got my own trophy to win.

956
01:06:49,853 --> 01:06:52,242
Now I'm going.

957
01:06:57,053 --> 01:07:01,604
Here come the Purple Cobras,
led by White Goodman. All business.

958
01:07:01,693 --> 01:07:05,129
We haven't seen Average Joe's yet.
They haven't made it to the court.

959
01:07:05,213 --> 01:07:08,603
It could be a psychological ploy,
or something worse.

960
01:07:08,693 --> 01:07:12,925
They're definitely not on the court, Cotton.
Their absence is noticeable.

961
01:07:13,013 --> 01:07:17,609
We'll be right back
after these words from our sponsors...

962
01:07:19,213 --> 01:07:21,443
Can I get a bottle of water?

963
01:07:23,853 --> 01:07:26,083
Aren't you Peter La Fleur?

964
01:07:27,093 --> 01:07:30,688
- Lance Armstrong?
- Yeah, that's me. But I'm a big fan of yours.

965
01:07:30,773 --> 01:07:34,482
- Really?
- Yeah, I've been watching the dodgeball.

966
01:07:34,573 --> 01:07:39,363
I just can't get enough of it. I'm really pullin'
for you against those jerks from Globo Gym.

967
01:07:39,973 --> 01:07:43,249
I think you better hurry up
or you're gonna be late.

968
01:07:43,333 --> 01:07:47,645
- Actually, I decided to quit, Lance.
- Quit?

969
01:07:48,453 --> 01:07:54,323
Once I thought of quittin', when I had brain,
lung and testicular cancer at the same time.

970
01:07:55,013 --> 01:07:57,686
But with the support of my friends
I got back on the bike

971
01:07:57,773 --> 01:08:00,367
and I won the Tour de France
five times in a row.

972
01:08:00,453 --> 01:08:04,332
But I'm sure you have a good reason to quit.

973
01:08:04,413 --> 01:08:07,803
What are you dying from
that's keepin' you from the finals?

974
01:08:07,893 --> 01:08:11,932
Right now, it feels a little bit like shame.

975
01:08:12,013 --> 01:08:17,610
If people never quit when the going got tough
they'd have nothing to regret all their lives.

976
01:08:17,693 --> 01:08:22,483
Good luck to you, Peter. I'm sure
this decision won't haunt you forever.

977
01:08:28,693 --> 01:08:32,606
Steve? Steve the Pirate? "Scurvy."

978
01:08:32,693 --> 01:08:36,732
- No. Not ringing any bells.
- Forget it, man.

979
01:08:36,813 --> 01:08:40,931
We'll play with four people. It's not
an advantage. Can't you bend the rules?

980
01:08:41,013 --> 01:08:45,211
There's nothing I can do. Rules are rules.
You don't have enough players.

981
01:08:45,293 --> 01:08:49,172
Inform the committee and Mr Goodman
about Average Joe's forfeit.

982
01:08:49,253 --> 01:08:52,404
- Yes, sir.
- Better luck next year.

983
01:08:54,013 --> 01:08:55,526
Excuse me.

984
01:08:55,613 --> 01:08:58,923
Sorry I'm late. You won't believe
whatjust happened. Hey, guys.

985
01:08:59,013 --> 01:09:01,686
You're just in time to help us forfeit.

986
01:09:01,773 --> 01:09:03,764
Forfeit? Why?

987
01:09:05,573 --> 01:09:08,645
Well, I don't know what to tell you, but...

988
01:09:08,733 --> 01:09:12,612
Yes, I'm being told that Average Joe's
does not have enough players

989
01:09:12,693 --> 01:09:15,526
and will be forfeiting
the championship match.

990
01:09:15,613 --> 01:09:18,571
It's a bold strategy, Cotton.
Let's see if it pays off for 'em.

991
01:09:18,653 --> 01:09:24,125
To the tournament floor we go, for the sceptre
presentation from the Dodgeball Chancellor.

992
01:09:24,213 --> 01:09:27,842
Ladies and gentlemen,
by the power vested in me

993
01:09:27,933 --> 01:09:32,961
by our governing body, the American
Dodgeball Association of America,

994
01:09:33,053 --> 01:09:37,569
and in concurrence with our sponsors,
Lumber Liquidators and Omaha Steaks,

995
01:09:37,653 --> 01:09:39,723
it gives me great pleasure

996
01:09:39,813 --> 01:09:44,523
to declare the winner of this year's
Las Vegas International Tournament to be...

997
01:09:44,613 --> 01:09:46,763
Wait. He's here.

998
01:09:51,053 --> 01:09:53,726
Hey, guys. Sorry I'm late.

999
01:09:53,813 --> 01:09:55,849
We're ready to play, Your Honour.

1000
01:09:55,933 --> 01:10:00,688
Too late. Your lovable band of losers already
forfeited. The trophy and money are mine.

1001
01:10:00,773 --> 01:10:04,129
He's right. The team already forfeited.
There's nothing you can do.

1002
01:10:04,213 --> 01:10:06,773
Facial, La Fleur. Total facial.

1003
01:10:07,893 --> 01:10:09,690
Actually, that's not true.

1004
01:10:09,773 --> 01:10:13,891
The committee can overrule the chancellor -
that's you, sir - by a two-thirds vote.

1005
01:10:13,973 --> 01:10:16,203
He's right. He's right. It's a bylaw.

1006
01:10:18,293 --> 01:10:20,807
- It's a bylaw.
- What's a bylaw?

1007
01:10:21,773 --> 01:10:25,209
- Hang on a second here, folks.
- Let them play.

1008
01:10:25,293 --> 01:10:29,047
We mightjust have a championship game yet.

1009
01:10:29,133 --> 01:10:32,091
Listen to this crowd.

1010
01:10:32,173 --> 01:10:34,289
Unbelievable.

1011
01:10:34,373 --> 01:10:39,493
Pepper, it's clear what the crowd wants, but
the committee members have the final say.

1012
01:10:39,573 --> 01:10:42,690
And it looks like they've come to a decision.

1013
01:10:42,773 --> 01:10:45,446
Joe's needs two "yes" votes to play.

1014
01:10:45,533 --> 01:10:48,809
- There's a thumbs-up. Good news for Joe's.
- Please.

1015
01:10:48,893 --> 01:10:51,965
- Let's see how our second judge votes.
- Thank you.

1016
01:10:52,053 --> 01:10:58,925
Oh, tough sledding there. It's all even. Their
fate hangs on the thumb of our final judge.

1017
01:10:59,013 --> 01:11:02,369
Thumbs up. Average Joe's can play.

1018
01:11:02,453 --> 01:11:05,604
That is pure poppycock.
You're gonna let them do that?

1019
01:11:05,693 --> 01:11:09,049
- Thank you, Chuck Norris.
- Thank you, Peter.

1020
01:11:10,773 --> 01:11:14,288
All right, captains. Shake hands,
and let's have a clean match.

1021
01:11:14,373 --> 01:11:16,364
Good luck, White.

1022
01:11:17,813 --> 01:11:20,885
Cram it up your cramhole, La Fleur.

1023
01:11:20,973 --> 01:11:24,283
Prepare to be humiliated on cable television.

1024
01:11:24,373 --> 01:11:26,364
Whatever.

1025
01:11:28,253 --> 01:11:31,325
- Nice of you to show up.
- Yeah, I thought so too.

1026
01:11:31,413 --> 01:11:34,211
What? I got a plan.

1027
01:11:36,053 --> 01:11:41,844
Let's play smart. Wait for two-on-ones. Cover
closely for your pick-ups. What's our motto?

1028
01:11:41,933 --> 01:11:44,049
- "Aim low".
- That's right.

1029
01:11:44,133 --> 01:11:47,011
All I'm asking is that
you give it your best for Patches.

1030
01:11:47,093 --> 01:11:51,211
I say we go out there, let it all hang loose,
try to have some fun.

1031
01:11:51,293 --> 01:11:53,853
I mean, it's only dodgeball, right?

1032
01:11:53,933 --> 01:11:57,812
- Put 'em in. One, two, three.
- Joe's.

1033
01:12:20,493 --> 01:12:22,688
Globo Gym, ready?

1034
01:12:22,773 --> 01:12:25,571
Average Joe's, ready?

1035
01:12:27,773 --> 01:12:28,728
Dodgeball.

1036
01:12:28,813 --> 01:12:34,046
Championship match is under way.
Average Joe's versus the Globo Gym Goliath.

1037
01:12:35,293 --> 01:12:37,932
Quick elimination there for Kate Veatch.

1038
01:12:39,213 --> 01:12:42,330
White Goodman's hit,
but that ball's up for grabs. And...

1039
01:12:42,413 --> 01:12:44,290
- It's caught.
- That's a catch.

1040
01:12:44,373 --> 01:12:47,809
- You're out, La Fleur.
- Peter La Fleur has gotta sit down.

1041
01:12:47,893 --> 01:12:51,010
And Joe's has lost
their two best players early.

1042
01:12:51,373 --> 01:12:53,443
Dwight Baumgarten still playing hard.

1043
01:12:53,533 --> 01:12:56,093
Hits Me'Shell Jones right on the dome.

1044
01:12:56,173 --> 01:12:58,084
You're mine next time.

1045
01:13:01,293 --> 01:13:06,083
Right in the tokus.
2-1, <i>ese,</i> and Globo Gym is dominating.

1046
01:13:09,973 --> 01:13:12,328
- Hi.
- Hey.

1047
01:13:14,133 --> 01:13:16,806
- You're out.
- I don't know what that was,

1048
01:13:16,893 --> 01:13:21,489
but it leaves Joe's on the wrong side
of a 4-2 advantage.

1049
01:13:21,573 --> 01:13:24,485
Joe's gets an elimination. It's two on three.

1050
01:13:24,573 --> 01:13:26,131
Get out.

1051
01:13:26,213 --> 01:13:28,488
Gordo. Lose your temper. Get mad.

1052
01:13:30,373 --> 01:13:34,366
White Goodman with a catch. Gordon Pibb
goes out, Me'Shell Jones comes back in.

1053
01:13:34,453 --> 01:13:36,171
You're out, four-eyes.

1054
01:13:36,253 --> 01:13:40,531
Well, it's all up to Average Joe's youngest
member. He's gotta make a play here, Pepper.

1055
01:13:40,613 --> 01:13:42,251
Word, Cotton.

1056
01:13:42,333 --> 01:13:47,487
Four Cobras and one Joe. Even a rabid
mongoose wouldn't have a chance now.

1057
01:13:47,573 --> 01:13:50,212
- Nice dodge.
- Stay alive. Stay alive.

1058
01:13:52,213 --> 01:13:54,522
They're just toying with the young man now.

1059
01:13:54,613 --> 01:13:57,446
He's gotta avoid getting hit. That's the key.

1060
01:13:57,533 --> 01:13:59,285
Justin, let's go.

1061
01:14:00,453 --> 01:14:01,932
What a great catch.

1062
01:14:02,013 --> 01:14:05,244
And another.
Peter La Fleur comes back into the game.

1063
01:14:05,333 --> 01:14:09,212
Just like that, a three-player swing.
Joe's isn't done yet.

1064
01:14:09,293 --> 01:14:10,851
Justin.

1065
01:14:10,933 --> 01:14:13,401
I love you.

1066
01:14:13,493 --> 01:14:15,324
I love you t...

1067
01:14:16,013 --> 01:14:17,969
Joanie loves Chachi.

1068
01:14:18,053 --> 01:14:21,648
Two players left on each side.
What a match. What a sport.

1069
01:14:22,253 --> 01:14:27,725
Throw out the rule book, folks,
it's down and dirty now. Street dodgeball.

1070
01:14:29,373 --> 01:14:33,048
Look out. La Fleur goes down -
he's a sitting duck.

1071
01:14:37,933 --> 01:14:43,849
How about that, folks? Kate Veatch takes the
bullet for Peter La Fleur. Now that's sacrifice.

1072
01:14:43,933 --> 01:14:48,688
As touching a moment as we've seen
on the dodgeball court all tournament.

1073
01:14:49,453 --> 01:14:52,013
A blatant cheap shot from White Goodman.

1074
01:14:52,093 --> 01:14:56,609
- That's court misconduct. That's a warning.
- Come on. Gimme a break.

1075
01:14:57,693 --> 01:14:59,172
- You OK?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

1076
01:14:59,253 --> 01:15:01,642
- Jesus. Are you sure?
- Yeah. I'm all right.

1077
01:15:01,733 --> 01:15:04,770
- It was an accident. I thought she was in play.
- Not a chance.

1078
01:15:04,853 --> 01:15:07,765
We're sweating like greased monkeys.
I can't hold on to a ball.

1079
01:15:07,853 --> 01:15:10,970
Sorry, miss, but you're out.
You gotta get off the court.

1080
01:15:11,053 --> 01:15:12,771
Watch him, man.

1081
01:15:12,853 --> 01:15:15,083
- Hey, Peter.
- Yeah?

1082
01:15:15,173 --> 01:15:16,891
Kick his ass.

1083
01:15:17,453 --> 01:15:20,490
- Here's the restart.
- Players, to your positions.

1084
01:15:20,573 --> 01:15:24,885
Looks like it's gonna be a two-on-one,
a <i>ménage à trois</i> of pain.

1085
01:15:24,973 --> 01:15:28,568
Usually you pay double
for that kind of action, Cotton.

1086
01:15:30,453 --> 01:15:34,048
You're playing ready dodgeball.
Balls are at your feet.

1087
01:15:34,133 --> 01:15:36,363
Ready? Dodgeball.

1088
01:15:36,453 --> 01:15:41,368
It's a cat-and-mouse game, folks.
Peter La Fleur has gotta wait for his shot.

1089
01:15:44,693 --> 01:15:47,127
He gets the elimination.

1090
01:15:48,293 --> 01:15:53,811
My. Globo Gym wins.
A Cinderella story cast asunder.

1091
01:15:53,893 --> 01:15:57,852
Average Joe's has come all this way
for nothing. Absolutely nothing.

1092
01:15:57,933 --> 01:16:00,572
They're not gonna get anything, Cotton.

1093
01:16:01,693 --> 01:16:05,652
No elimination. Double fault.
You stepped over the line on the throw.

1094
01:16:05,733 --> 01:16:09,612
What? You gotta be out of your mind.
That is the worst call I've ever seen.

1095
01:16:09,693 --> 01:16:13,891
I'm out here busting my butt and you come in
with a bush-league call like that? Bullcrap.

1096
01:16:13,973 --> 01:16:18,808
ADAA Continuation Rule 113-D, sir.
Sudden death.

1097
01:16:18,893 --> 01:16:20,292
All right. Bring it.

1098
01:16:20,373 --> 01:16:23,683
I don't believe it, folks. Sudden death.

1099
01:16:23,773 --> 01:16:25,445
Well, let me tell you,

1100
01:16:25,533 --> 01:16:31,130
a double-fault final-play elimination hasn't
occurred since the Helsinki episode of 1919,

1101
01:16:31,213 --> 01:16:33,852
and I think we all remember
how that turned out.

1102
01:16:33,933 --> 01:16:40,327
Ladies and gentlemen, it's the greatest
happening in sport. Sudden-death dodgeball.

1103
01:16:40,413 --> 01:16:42,722
Pepper needs new shorts.

1104
01:16:44,653 --> 01:16:47,770
White, Peter, this is sudden death.

1105
01:16:48,213 --> 01:16:53,571
Only striking an opposing player eliminates
them. Catching the ball does nothing.

1106
01:16:53,653 --> 01:16:57,487
Both feet must remain
in the triangle at all times.

1107
01:16:57,573 --> 01:17:02,089
You may throw any time after my call.
Understood?

1108
01:17:02,973 --> 01:17:06,648
OK. Let's have a clean match.
Good luck, gentlemen.

1109
01:17:07,133 --> 01:17:09,931
This is it, La Loser.

1110
01:17:11,333 --> 01:17:14,882
You ready for the hurricane?

1111
01:17:15,933 --> 01:17:19,528
Just don't go cryin' to mama when
I spank you in front of all these people.

1112
01:17:20,653 --> 01:17:25,488
You don't go crying to your daddy
after I wipe it up with your face.

1113
01:17:27,053 --> 01:17:29,851
- White?
- Yeah?

1114
01:17:29,933 --> 01:17:34,370
- You look awful fat in those pants.
- Players, to your positions.

1115
01:17:34,453 --> 01:17:38,082
This is about gamesmanship.
Throw early and you're defenceless.

1116
01:17:38,173 --> 01:17:44,009
Throw late and you're eliminated.
Dilemma, thy name is dodgeball.

1117
01:17:44,093 --> 01:17:47,085
This sport doesn't build character,
it reveals it.

1118
01:17:47,173 --> 01:17:50,131
Effin' A, Cotton. Effin' A.

1119
01:17:51,893 --> 01:17:53,884
Come on, talk to me.

1120
01:17:55,413 --> 01:17:57,563
Listen up, crotch stain.

1121
01:17:57,653 --> 01:18:01,851
Remember your training
and trust your instincts.

1122
01:18:01,933 --> 01:18:04,606
You can do it. I believe in you.

1123
01:18:07,413 --> 01:18:09,131
Bye-bye.

1124
01:18:09,213 --> 01:18:10,202
Right.

1125
01:18:10,293 --> 01:18:13,091
Players, turn and step in.

1126
01:18:28,213 --> 01:18:30,681
What the hell's he doing?

1127
01:18:30,773 --> 01:18:33,287
I don't know.

1128
01:18:35,333 --> 01:18:36,527
Get a load of this guy.

1129
01:18:36,613 --> 01:18:40,242
In 23 years of broadcasting
I thought I'd seen it all, folks.

1130
01:18:40,333 --> 01:18:44,087
But it looks like Peter La Fleur
has actually blindfolded himself.

1131
01:18:44,173 --> 01:18:46,846
He will not be able to see very well, Cotton.

1132
01:18:56,013 --> 01:18:58,481
Ready?

1133
01:19:03,093 --> 01:19:05,448
Dodgeball.

1134
01:19:11,213 --> 01:19:13,408
Goodbye, Peter.

1135
01:19:13,493 --> 01:19:16,212
I always knew you were weak.

1136
01:19:19,573 --> 01:19:22,246
Air Goodman, comin' at ya.

1137
01:19:29,773 --> 01:19:32,765
Down goes Goodman.
Down goes Goodman.

1138
01:19:32,853 --> 01:19:36,050
Winner. Average Joe's.

1139
01:19:39,373 --> 01:19:42,922
Do you believe in unlikelihoods?

1140
01:19:43,013 --> 01:19:46,130
Average Joe's shocking the dodgeball world

1141
01:19:46,213 --> 01:19:50,252
and upsetting Globo Gym
in the championship match.

1142
01:19:50,333 --> 01:19:51,652
Unbelievable.

1143
01:19:51,733 --> 01:19:56,011
I have been to the Great Wall of China.
I have seen the Pyramids of Egypt.

1144
01:19:56,093 --> 01:19:58,607
I've even witnessed a grown man
satisfy a camel.

1145
01:19:58,693 --> 01:20:00,923
But never in all my years as a sportscaster

1146
01:20:01,013 --> 01:20:05,962
have I witnessed something as improbable,
as impossible, as what we've witnessed here.

1147
01:20:06,053 --> 01:20:10,649
The little team that could, Average Joe's
Gymnasium, underdogs throughout,

1148
01:20:10,733 --> 01:20:15,409
stand before us, aglow,
as true dodgeball champions.

1149
01:20:15,493 --> 01:20:19,964
On behalf of the American Dodgeball
Association of America,

1150
01:20:20,053 --> 01:20:24,365
it is my honour to present to you
this cheque for $50,000.

1151
01:20:30,373 --> 01:20:33,331
What are you so happy about, La Fleur?
None of this matters.

1152
01:20:33,413 --> 01:20:37,725
You signed your gym over to me last night,
remember? You lost, I won.

1153
01:20:37,813 --> 01:20:39,883
Suck failure, freaks.

1154
01:20:39,973 --> 01:20:43,090
Peter, is that true?

1155
01:20:43,173 --> 01:20:45,084
Yeah, it's true.

1156
01:20:45,173 --> 01:20:48,370
It's true I sold Average Joe's to White.

1157
01:20:48,453 --> 01:20:50,808
It's true that every man has his price.

1158
01:20:50,893 --> 01:20:55,683
And it's also true that money won
is a lot sweeter than money earned.

1159
01:20:55,773 --> 01:20:59,971
- Now he's a philosophiser.
- Excuse us. Step aside, please.

1160
01:21:01,053 --> 01:21:03,362
Your winnings, Mr La Fleur.
Congratulations.

1161
01:21:03,453 --> 01:21:07,332
- Right on time. I appreciate it. Thank you.
- What is that? What winnings?

1162
01:21:07,413 --> 01:21:11,884
Gosh, I totally forgot to tell you. I took the
$100,000 bribe that you gave me last night,

1163
01:21:11,973 --> 01:21:14,931
and I put it on us to win.
We were going off at 50-1.

1164
01:21:15,013 --> 01:21:18,289
Anyone? Top of your head?
What's 50 times $100,000?

1165
01:21:18,373 --> 01:21:19,726
$50,000?

1166
01:21:19,813 --> 01:21:23,726
$5 million. Peter, are you kidding me?

1167
01:21:23,813 --> 01:21:25,883
Surprise.

1168
01:21:29,053 --> 01:21:33,968
Stick it in your ear, La Fleur. I wouldn't sell
you your gym back for all King Midas's silver.

1169
01:21:34,053 --> 01:21:38,729
The gym is mine. So you can take your band
of yellow-bellied losers and crawl out of here.

1170
01:21:38,813 --> 01:21:41,646
You're right. I can't make you
sell Average Joe's to me.

1171
01:21:41,733 --> 01:21:45,408
So I guess I'll just take your advice
and invest in something.

1172
01:21:45,493 --> 01:21:49,566
- Say the controlling stake of Globo Gym.
- That's preposterous. I'd never allow it.

1173
01:21:49,653 --> 01:21:53,282
Globo Gym is a publicly traded company.
There's nothing you can do about it.

1174
01:21:53,373 --> 01:21:58,606
So I would control Globo Gym
and everything that Globo Gym owns,

1175
01:21:58,693 --> 01:22:02,686
which, as of last night, is Average Joe's Gym.

1176
01:22:04,013 --> 01:22:05,412
I'm your new boss, White.

1177
01:22:05,493 --> 01:22:08,769
You can't be my boss. Nobody can.
I'm my own boss. I created myself.

1178
01:22:08,853 --> 01:22:11,925
- You're fired, pal.
- You can't do anything to me.

1179
01:22:12,453 --> 01:22:15,411
You're going down, La Fleur,
like a sweet muffin.

1180
01:22:15,493 --> 01:22:18,963
- Another time, another time.
- You suck, La Fleur.

1181
01:22:20,773 --> 01:22:22,764
Give me that.

1182
01:22:25,533 --> 01:22:28,001
Man, the blindfold was crazy.

1183
01:22:29,453 --> 01:22:31,967
Peter.

1184
01:22:32,053 --> 01:22:34,521
Look. It's Steve the Pirate.

1185
01:22:38,013 --> 01:22:43,007
I just wanted to tell you
that I thought about what you said, and

1186
01:22:44,013 --> 01:22:46,243
I guess you're right.

1187
01:22:46,333 --> 01:22:48,608
I'm not really a pirate.

1188
01:22:49,893 --> 01:22:52,361
I don't know, Steve.

1189
01:22:52,453 --> 01:22:54,569
If you're not a pirate,

1190
01:22:54,653 --> 01:22:58,362
who the hell am I gonna split
all that buried treasure with?

1191
01:23:03,293 --> 01:23:05,090
Peter...

1192
01:23:05,173 --> 01:23:06,970
Gar, Steve.

1193
01:23:12,293 --> 01:23:13,885
We missed you.

1194
01:23:16,773 --> 01:23:18,365
Hey, you.

1195
01:23:18,453 --> 01:23:20,444
Hey, you.

1196
01:23:22,093 --> 01:23:24,049
- Joyce?
- Kate.

1197
01:23:24,493 --> 01:23:28,771
- I thought you were in Guam.
- I caught an early flight. I wouldn't miss this.

1198
01:23:28,853 --> 01:23:31,048
You are amazing.

1199
01:23:34,573 --> 01:23:38,964
- I told you she was a lesbian.
- Wow. Good call.

1200
01:23:39,453 --> 01:23:42,445
Hey. I'm not a lesbian.

1201
01:23:42,533 --> 01:23:44,125
You're not?

1202
01:23:44,213 --> 01:23:45,692
No.

1203
01:23:45,773 --> 01:23:48,128
I'm bisexual.

1204
01:23:49,693 --> 01:23:51,524
Snap.

1205
01:23:52,093 --> 01:23:55,449
All right, everybody. Smile big.

1206
01:24:00,133 --> 01:24:03,887
Hi. I'm Peter La Fleur,
owner and operator of Average Joe's Gym.

1207
01:24:03,973 --> 01:24:07,488
I'm here to tell you
you're perfectjust the way you are.

1208
01:24:07,573 --> 01:24:13,045
But if you feel like losin' a few pounds, gettin'
healthier, and makin' friends in the process,

1209
01:24:13,133 --> 01:24:14,885
Joe's is the place for you.

1210
01:24:14,973 --> 01:24:18,283
Don't forget that youth dodgeball classes
are forming right now.

1211
01:24:18,373 --> 01:24:23,049
So come on down and learn a great game the
way it's supposed to be played. Right, kids?

1212
01:24:23,133 --> 01:24:25,124
Right.

1213
01:24:34,253 --> 01:24:36,289
Spare me.

1214
01:24:36,373 --> 01:24:38,762
I won that tournament.

1215
01:24:41,333 --> 01:24:44,052
Fucking Chuck Norris.

1216
01:24:46,053 --> 01:24:48,044
Visiontext Subtitles:
Julie Clayton & Rob Colling

1217
01:24:48,293 --> 01:24:50,284
ENGLISH

1218
01:27:42,013 --> 01:27:45,050
Yeah. I hope you're all happy now.

1219
01:27:45,133 --> 01:27:47,567
Good guy wins, bad guy loses.

1220
01:27:47,653 --> 01:27:50,121
Big friggin' surprise.

1221
01:27:51,173 --> 01:27:53,084
I love happy endings.

1222
01:27:55,973 --> 01:28:00,171
You know, that's the problem
with the American cinema.

1223
01:28:00,253 --> 01:28:02,642
Can't handle any complexity in it, you know?

1224
01:28:02,733 --> 01:28:06,772
"Don't make me think,
I just wanna be entertained."

1225
01:28:06,853 --> 01:28:08,684
All right, fine.

1226
01:28:08,773 --> 01:28:12,288
You want a little somethin'-somethin'
for the ride home?

1227
01:28:12,373 --> 01:28:14,762
Check these boots out for size.

1228
01:28:16,533 --> 01:28:18,649
My milkshake brings all the boys to the yard

1229
01:28:18,733 --> 01:28:20,803
And they're like, "It's better than yours"

1230
01:28:20,893 --> 01:28:22,770
Damn right, it's better than yours

1231
01:28:22,853 --> 01:28:25,413
I could teach you, but I'd have to charge

1232
01:28:26,413 --> 01:28:30,406
What the boys go crazy for

1233
01:28:31,693 --> 01:28:32,808
They lose their minds

1234
01:28:32,893 --> 01:28:35,168
My milkshake brings all the boys to the yard

1235
01:28:35,253 --> 01:28:36,971
Damn right, it's better than yours

1236
01:28:37,053 --> 01:28:40,523
I could teach you, but I'd have to charge

1237
01:28:42,173 --> 01:28:45,131
You happy? Fatty make a funny?
